What happened? Well, the classic EQ itemization paradigm treats Archery the same as 2H weapons, but discounts the arrow entirely - reasons are for the reader to divine. This results in a damage potential that's actually rather insane - in practice players can acquire a max level arrow, a simple bow, and be rocking archery far above their weight class because of the way the calculations work. Rather than assault you further with copious sheets of data, I want to point out that as of July 24, 2026, archery is actually quite impressive. Use the methodology described here to find your own breakpoints, but the rule to follow that if your bow+arrow is better than a comparable 2H/DW rig, it's archery time.

